# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. A crash a fuzz run finds is only
# reproducible if the inputs map to the same values later, and `arbitrary`
# decides that mapping — a minor bump can change what a stored corpus byte
# string decodes to, so a reproducer can quietly stop reproducing. Pinning the
# lock keeps "this input crashed on this tree" durable. The crate's own
# Cargo.lock is tracked for the same reason.
